 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- **Occlusion:** Projected points may be occluded in reference images, leading to inaccurate color retrieval. The source mentions using geometric priors (visibility maps based on depth differences) to mitigate this during training, but the initialization step itself relies directly on the projected colors [S1].
-- **Fixed Radius:** The radius $r_{bg}$ is fixed at 100 m. If the scene scale differs significantly, this may lead to poor background representation [S1].
-- **Fixed Rotation/Opacity:** Since rotation and opacity are not learned, the model assumes a specific orientation and full transparency for background Gaussians, which may not hold for all background structures [S1].
